  "summary_en": "An IFR member blog post by the chair of the Russian Association of Robotics outlines five trends in Russian robotics: government digital-economy support, educational robotics, a growing service robot sector, the industrial robot market, and robots for SMEs. It mentions planned AI and robotics regulation meant to reduce legal risk, and a state-funded R&D roadmap.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "The 2017 Digital Economy programme includes robotics initiatives, and RAR is drafting a robotics industry strategy with the Ministry of Trade and Industry",
   "The government plans AI and robotics regulation to clarify legal issues and reduce legal risk; in 2018 it commissioned RoboLaw-style research",
   "An R&D roadmap defines which priority robotics technologies will receive state funding",
   "Educational robotics is booming; in 2017 education accounted for 31% of service robot sales",
   "Industrial robot density is low (4 per 10,000 workers), and Robot-as-a-Service and cobots help SMEs adopt robots"
